      "explanation": "Explanation:\nTo move the green cube (obj0) closer to the red cylinder (obj4), we first determine their current positions: obj0 at [0.146, 0.005] and obj4 at [0.044, -0.206]. We then compute the direction vector from obj0 to obj4: [0.044, -0.206] - [0.146, 0.005] = [-0.102, -0.211]. We calculate the distance between them: sqrt((-0.102)^2 + (-0.211)^2) = 0.229. \n\nWe then choose an interpolation factor \u03b1 \u2208 [0, 1] and move obj0 along the direction vector. Let's try \u03b1 = 0.5 which gives us a move offset of [-0.051, -0.1055]. Adding this offset to the current position of obj0 gives us a new position of [0.095, -0.1005]. \n\nWe then check the distance between the new position of obj0 and obj4: sqrt((0.095 - 0.044)^2 + (-0.1005 - (-0.206))^2) = 0.114. This is less than the original distance, so obj0 is indeed closer to obj4. However, the distance is less than 0.075, so we need to reduce \u03b1. Let's try \u03b1 = 0.3 which gives us a move offset of [-0.0306, -0.0633] and a new position for obj0 of [0.1154, -0.0583]. \n\nThe distance between this new position and obj4 is sqrt((0.1154 - 0.044)^2 + (-0.0583 - (-0.206))^2) = 0.137 which is greater than 0.075 and less than the original distance, so this is a valid position. \n\nThe symbolic plan is then to move the robot arm to obj0, pick it up, move it to the new position, and release it.",
